				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5133</guid>
				<title>SCP-5133</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5133</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Object class: &lt;strong&gt;Keter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Containment measures&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5133 is to be kept in a tall cell made out of 100% marble. The cell should be at least 25 feet high. Windows and a trapdoor are located at the top, since SCP-5133 cannot climb. For any repairs, the SCP should be stunned with a medium sized bomb (dropped into the cell via trapdoor). SCP-5133 should NEVER be let out of its cell. There is NO EXCEPTION to this rule.
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5133 is a golden colored outdoor hot tub with small legs. It appears to be sentient. The wires on the bottom secrete a oily liquid that is highly corrosive to everything except marble. However, the water inside can corrode through everything &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;except for its cover.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;Its cover should be on at ALL TIMES.&lt;/span&gt; The water instantly kills humans on touch. When a human is in its cell, they will feel an urge to touch the water. Tests show it promises to &amp;quot;heal any wound&amp;quot;. However, SCP-5133 cannot talk as it has no eyes or mouth. It seems to have a nose on the underside though. It also modifies anything written, typed, or talked about &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;lifting the cover.&lt;/span&gt; Bombs have shown to stun the SCP for up to a month (depending on the size).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;end-of-the-world-scenario&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
If ever in contact with the ocean, SCP-5133 will summon a wave and jump to it. The wave will expand at a high rate, eventually crushing everything in its path. Therefore, SCP-5133 is located in ███████, away from the ocean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5133 was found on a small island where humans lived. The last thing heard from the island before a &amp;quot;large tsunami&amp;quot; hit the island was &amp;quot;There&#039;s a&amp;#8230;. a&amp;#8230;. Hot tub???&amp;quot;. Agents soon investigated the area and found SCP-5133 in a small shack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I may add interviews and stuff later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacknackbackpack&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7170671&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1609057197&quot; alt=&quot;jacknackbackpack&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7170671)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacknackbackpack&quot;  &gt;jacknackbackpack&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 27 Dec 2020 02:28:16 +0000</pubDate>
